lee-texparts.js, lee-board.js, lee-board.css, board/rough.js and board/perfect-freehand.mjs: the screen guide's formula parts and board, copied unchanged from abhyasa 0.0.15 from PyPI, wheel abhyasa-0.0.15-py3-none-any.whl, SHA-256 dcc968bd1c7d09b7bd2486b902c67ea3bb94f521d08c25189b324613b7dd3ae6. The source files are abhyasa/core/texparts.js, abhyasa/core/board.js, abhyasa/core/board.css, abhyasa/core/vendor/rough.js and abhyasa/core/vendor/perfect-freehand.mjs. pyproject.toml pins abhyasa to this wheel. tests/test_vendor_board.py compares each file with the file in the installed wheel. board/ is the folder the page passes to the board as `host.assets`, served at /leestatic/board/. board/LICENSES.md is abhyasa's licence file for the two libraries. Download the wheel into an empty folder, check the digest, extract it into another folder, then copy the files:

    d=$(mktemp -d) && curl -sS -o "$d/abhyasa-0.0.15-py3-none-any.whl" https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/62/b4/31bdafa8fec2b2235b49cd35d1a66af41a1d79201e03936f01ad873b4102/abhyasa-0.0.15-py3-none-any.whl && shasum -a 256 "$d/abhyasa-0.0.15-py3-none-any.whl"
    e=$(mktemp -d) && unzip -q "$d/abhyasa-0.0.15-py3-none-any.whl" -d "$e" && c="$e/abhyasa/core" && cp "$c/texparts.js" leela/vendor/lee-texparts.js && cp "$c/board.js" leela/vendor/lee-board.js && cp "$c/board.css" leela/vendor/lee-board.css && cp "$c/vendor/rough.js" "$c/vendor/perfect-freehand.mjs" "$c/vendor/LICENSES.md" leela/vendor/board/

